# Independent canonical page-context implementation review

Review only. Root owns implementation, specifications and Git changes. All independent probes were appended to isolated Git-blob snapshots under this directory; the production worktree was not edited. Final fixed14df7e9d77faa86715c4605b28a853812980c4b0 has no outstanding blocking finding within this bounded review. Earlier defects and failed probes remain separately identified below.

## Fixed sources and scope

Initial implementation 87ce544168a808918a01608b02a73f577a9f8caf, base e45323ff136cbd7be488ab697af9b555a0d3df26. Follow-ups ce0b520850822e199178518f241785ca6c608d53, 37cfaa88149191e1e066b08682720f5df471cf2d, and 819f0e9a7d983bb8b104f1dceb5681989e046369 are separately frozen with their exact source bytes, patches, allowlists and dependency hashes. 8981ba013618c38232fee58ea00b8b479d17ca74 adds one managed regression to tests.rs only; its production equals 819. The later chapter22 source/registry/archive integration in ce is identified separately in final/snapshot.json and is not an archive review here.

Final14df7e9d77faa86715c4605b28a853812980c4b0 differs from819 only in canonical.rs (the thirteen-line file-ancestor check) and tests.rs. final14df records these exact blobs. Every unchanged production dependency and the explicitly appended final probe overlay were rechecked by verify_final.py; 674 dependency paths are accounted for.

Directly inspected canonical.rs, canonical/projection.rs, annotated/host.rs, CLI dispatch and managed tests; the existing typed annotated/pages renderer, Doc PageSet resolution, filesystem staging implementation, specification16/21 and the preceding independent design review. New authored16/21 content is another reviewer's scope. No raw plan, raw receipt or file existence is accepted as a checked PageSet proof.

The implementation captures bounded explicit registry/source/alias inputs, compiles real source into named owner scopes, resolves the complete PageSet, checks actual emitted anchors and renders without passive Markdown targets. Physical source, logical Markdown projection and HTML route have separate roles. Legacy /2 final bytes use the original namespace and generator after checking their bodies against the grouped result. Raw manifest bytes and all ordered per-page inputs enter a separate, length-framed context identity. The ordinary old-only --check retains sequential per-page operations; explicit staging has its documented finite aggregate limits. Parse/lower budgets remain per-page operations, and the selected output budget is shared by resolution/render/metadata. Capturing host files/JSON is bounded separately, not falsely described as core allocation metering.

## Executed independent evidence

Final819: native-819.command.json identifies the exact Windows x86_64 native command, dedicated target, 900-second process deadline, probe and executable hashes. Eight tests passed. check_records.py independently reconstructed the framed SHA-256 from raw input strings and verified 23 records, including seven exact sticky stop reasons. identity-819 adds one successful native test with ten input mutations and exact repeated files/receipt checks. prefix-819 is a separate observational reproduction of an operation failure, not a successful projection claim.

Final14df: native-14df.command.json records a fresh build and eleven independent native tests passing (72.05 seconds test execution). All previous eight probes, the ten identity mutations, the unchanged prefix reproduction and a new boundary test run together. Twenty-three context records again pass the independent Python digest/stop checker. The final four Markdown outputs AND their receipt exactly equal819's five artifacts. final-verification.json records the exact checks and the final prefix result.

The independently specified cases cover mutual and self links, Japanese semantic fragments, legacy aliases, distinct Markdown versus HTML directories, source-dependent identities for equal source text under different page IDs, stale stored Markdown rejection, existing output preservation, late malformed aliases/source, unregistered ambient Markdown and non-emitted anchors. Public markdown and check exercise all six zero resource limits and strict rejection of seven malformed limit values; omission of the complete optional limits field is accepted, null or sparse objects are not. The private helper separately exercises caller Work19, caller depth7, success-minus-one boundaries and cancelled/pre-stopped reruns. Decimal width of serialized limits is held stable for exact minus-one tests: receipt size itself depends on limits.

The 129-page old-only check passed, while explicit staging rejected its count before creating the output directory. Ten context mutations cover raw registry whitespace, registry path, source bytes/path, alias bytes/path, page ID, Markdown projection, HTML route and an explicitly supplied default limits object. Each changes the context hash; changes that do not affect the PageSet keep its digest stable. Header tokens in identity-819's raw log include their following punctuation; this is preserved and documented by verify_evidence.py, not misrepresented as 65-byte digests.

The actual fixed 00/13/22 sources and unchanged authored01 were compiled and rendered through public markdown with Work300,000,000 and Allocation750,000,000 selected before entry. Initial usage is zero; all other limits are recorded. All three existing legacy Markdown files exactly equal fixed Git blobs. The 01 output contains its actual relative link to 22 and its original doc-core/math-core statement. Four Markdown artifacts are identical between37 and819; the receipt's pre-serialization Work rises by396 for the corrected copy charges, with other recorded resource quantities unchanged. At819 the receipt reports Work188,404,774, Allocation494,156,717, Nodes7,678,688 before receipt serialization. This is not final operation usage and is not a default-budget success or chapter01 canonical cutover.

## Findings and repairs

Initial WIP concerns about old-only compatibility, context vector reallocation, metadata growth/hash costs, legacy output budget separation and receipt precharging were reported to root and corrected before the final probes. A fixed37 production reproduction with Work1 and page ID lengths16/2048 returned Allocation520/2552 despite stopping before registration publication. Root819 prepays copy Work before Allocation for registration strings and final output path clones. The unchanged independent probe now returns Allocation256 at both widths, preserving sticky WorkLimit and Work1. The original before output and executable/probe identities are retained.

Fixed819 reproduction: an old-only registry with projections doc/a.md and doc/a.md/b.md is accepted, writes the first file, then fails with Windows OS error183 creating the second parent directory. No completion manifest is emitted. This is not a false success, but a deterministically invalid output namespace should fail before writes; mixed/new PageSet resolution already rejects such prefixes. Root14df adds registry file-ancestor validation. The original input and raw failure are retained in prefix_probe.rs and prefix-819.*. The unchanged probe now reports registry_accepted=false, output_exists=false, first_file_exists=false and completion_exists=false, with the explicit canonical file path used as directory error. Ten further negative cases vary case, deep ancestry, page order and cross-field source/alias/projection relationships. The non-conflicting doc/a.md versus doc/a.md.other.md case succeeds with both files and completion manifest. The implementation uses the complete case-folded file set and checks every slash ancestor, so a lexicographic intervening name cannot hide a conflict. Existing legitimate file inputs and output bytes are retained.

## Limits and replay

No independent WASI/Linux/macOS run is claimed for this host filesystem operation. Prior typed PageSet cross-target evidence is a distinct scope. Symlink races, OS crashes during staging, deployment, passive Markdown HTML generation, human semantic acceptance and canonical migration completion are not established by these probes. A completed receipt is written last; physical I/O failures may leave an incomplete staging directory.

Earlier evidence remains phase-labelled: native-expanded is an independent probe compilation mistake; native-final initially supplied incomplete OutputLimits and correctly failed schema decoding. Both are retained and were corrected in probe code, not by relaxing production. Original87 runs and37 artifact evidence predate the final819 fixes. Initial-native-completion retains only the available tool result, not a complete reconstructed build transcript. Binary hashes added by the final runner are claimed only where command records contain them. The plan lists proposed cases, not additional executed coverage.

Replay uses the fixed Git dependency snapshots and only the named probe overlays. Build workspaces, caches and binaries are excluded from the final evidence allowlist; executable hashes remain in command records. verify_evidence.py checks the historical819 Git identities and emitted artifact bytes. To replay that stage, reconstruct it using freeze_final.py, update_37.py and update_819.py before run_final.py or run_identity.py; those historical runners alone do not restore later production deltas. To replay final14df, reconstruct819, apply update_14df.py, execute run_14df.py, check_records.py native-14df and verify_final.py. Do not run an earlier-labelled script over later sources. Preserve raw logs and earlier failures instead of overwriting the archived evidence when replaying.
